{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "If Forte is the vocal group's album, its classical crossover sound makes it my strongest choice because it connects closely with my listening to Il Divo and The Tenors.",
    "If 25 is Adele's album and A Wonderful World is Susan Boyle's, expressive singing and gentle, familiar songs give me clear reasons to choose them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me and PTXmas connect with my Christmas listening, but that connection does not make them what I want to hear today.",
    "New Moves / Traces, Heritage, and How Can It Be leave me unsure what I would hear, so I cannot confidently connect them with the vocal music I enjoy."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My past Christmas listening seems to have been treated as an ongoing preference, although I am not seeking holiday music now.",
    "My country listening explains some choices, but it does not mean I want country albums as much as classical crossover today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection among Il Divo, The Tenors, and my other vocal-focused listening matters especially strongly to my choices right now.",
    "My most recent relaxing classical selection suggests that a gentle sound deserves more weight than simply matching something I listened to years ago."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in vocal music, but give older holiday and country interests more weight than my current preference for classical crossover and relaxing listening."
}"}
